From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thuong Vo <66083331+SekiroKenjii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: add Apex's Graphics and Display group after Power Mode

Board 24 adds a Graphics and Display group to Power's General page:
the NVIDIA graphics card's power state, read from power/runtime_status,
and a switch for apex-desktop's lower-refresh-rate-on-battery key, with
the built-in display's rates from Mutter's DisplayConfig. The group is
panels/apex/cc-apex-power.c; the panel only hands it the page and the
group to follow. Stock's rows and pages stay as they are.
---
 panels/power/cc-power-panel.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/panels/power/cc-power-panel.c b/panels/power/cc-power-panel.c
index 8d7cbe7..8b6b22f 100644
--- a/panels/power/cc-power-panel.c
+++ b/panels/power/cc-power-panel.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include "cc-power-profile-row.h"
 #include "cc-power-resources.h"
 #include "cc-ui-util.h"
+#include "panels/apex/cc-apex-power.h"
 #include "shell/cc-object-storage.h"
 
 /* This enum represents the availability of power actions, ordered from least
@@ -1232,6 +1233,7 @@ cc_power_panel_init (CcPowerPanel *self)
                      "active", G_SETTINGS_BIND_DEFAULT);
 
     setup_general_section (self);
+    cc_apex_power_add (self->general_page, GTK_WIDGET (self->power_profile_section));
 
     /* populate batteries */
     if (self->up_client) {
